{"id":"m2://rec/open_logic/content/sets-functions-relations/relations/orders.tex#proof-3#1","source":"open_logic","snapshot":"blake3:a5eb116529d3e799289dd9f7e7530d0d446b3615f5608fe08c668241eee3c765","locator":"https://github.com/OpenLogicProject/OpenLogic/blob/1e960beff9ed7835bf3e3f1335e21af3439cd107/content/sets-functions-relations/relations/orders.tex#L162","native_id":"content/sets-functions-relations/relations/orders.tex#proof-3","kind":"proof","text":"Suppose $(\\forall x \\in A)(x < a \\liff x < b)$. If $a < b$, then $a <\na$, contradicting the fact that $<$ is irreflexive; so $a \\nless b$.\nExactly similarly, $b \\nless a$. So $a = b$, as $<$ is connected.","class":"open","by":"textbook/1","resource":"PKGMM3P5QY","at":{"section":"80.4","kind":"proof"}}
